## 2. Thematic Analysis

### 2.1 Theme 1: Setup Friction

| Attribute | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Theme ID** | T-01 |
| **Description** | The recurring effort required to set up configuration, fixtures, API clients, browser lifecycle, and CI reporting from scratch for every new project. |
| **Frequency** | Mentioned in **7 of 8** interviews (87.5%). |
| **Supporting Interviews** | U-001, U-002, U-004, U-005, U-006, U-008, U-009 |
| **Representative Quote** | *"I've built the same fixture setup three times in the last two years."* — U-001 |
| **Impact Description** | Causes 1–2 days of lost setup time per project; diverts effort from writing meaningful test coverage. |
| **Severity** | High |
| **Current Workaround** | Copy-paste from previous projects; maintain personal templates. |
| **ForgeQA Fit** | Directly addressable by a reusable framework with standard fixtures and configuration. |

### 2.2 Theme 2: Diagnostic Gaps

| Attribute | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Theme ID** | T-02 |
| **Description** | The lack of sufficient context (screenshots, traces, request/response metadata) to investigate why a test failed, leading to extended debugging time. |
| **Frequency** | Mentioned in **6 of 8** interviews (75%). |
| **Supporting Interviews** | U-001, U-003, U-004, U-005, U-007, U-009 |
| **Representative Quote** | *"We spend more time investigating why a test failed than writing new tests."* — U-001 |
| **Impact Description** | Causes 3–5 hours per week of investigation time; delays release decisions. |
| **Severity** | High |
| **Current Workaround** | Manual `print()` statements; re-running tests locally; ad-hoc screenshots. |
| **ForgeQA Fit** | Directly addressable by evidence-first diagnostics (screenshots, traces, structured logs). |

### 2.3 Theme 3: Flaky Test Investigation

| Attribute | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Theme ID** | T-03 |
| **Description** | Tests that pass and fail intermittently, causing distrust in the test suite and wasted time re-running pipelines. |
| **Frequency** | Mentioned in **5 of 8** interviews (62.5%). |
| **Supporting Interviews** | U-002, U-003, U-006, U-008, U-010 |
| **Representative Quote** | *"We have a list of 'known flaky' tests that we just re-run until they pass."* — U-003 |
| **Impact Description** | Causes 2–4 hours per week of re-runs; reduces confidence in CI results. |
| **Severity** | Medium-High |
| **Current Workaround** | Re-running failed tests; temporarily disabling flaky tests. |
| **ForgeQA Fit** | Partially addressable by isolation, timeouts, and retry history (Phase 5). |

### 2.4 Theme 4: Test Data Management

| Attribute | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Theme ID** | T-04 |
| **Description** | The difficulty of creating, isolating, and cleaning up test data, especially when tests run in parallel. |
| **Frequency** | Mentioned in **4 of 8** interviews (50%). |
| **Supporting Interviews** | U-002, U-005, U-007, U-009 |
| **Representative Quote** | *"Tests collide because they all use the same test user account."* — U-005 |
| **Impact Description** | Causes intermittent failures; requires manual cleanup; limits parallel execution. |
| **Severity** | Medium |
| **Current Workaround** | Hard-coded test data; manual database resets. |
| **ForgeQA Fit** | Partially addressable by test-data factories and isolation conventions (Phase 5). |

### 2.5 Theme 5: CI/CD Integration Complexity

| Attribute | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Theme ID** | T-05 |
| **Description** | The effort required to configure CI pipelines, manage secrets, and publish test results and artifacts. |
| **Frequency** | Mentioned in **3 of 8** interviews (37.5%). |
| **Supporting Interviews** | U-001, U-004, U-010 |
| **Representative Quote** | *"Getting the JUnit XML report into GitHub Actions was a two-day task."* — U-004 |
| **Impact Description** | Causes 1–2 days of initial setup; ongoing maintenance burden. |
| **Severity** | Medium |
| **Current Workaround** | Copy-paste CI YAML from previous projects. |
